'''Verlo Skiff''' was a [[human]] [[Gender|male]] who served the [[Pre-Mor Security Inspection team|law enforcement arm]] of [[Consolidated Holdings of Preox-Morlana Corporation|Preox-Morlana]] on [[Morlana One]]<ref name="Episode 1" /> as a [[Tac-Corpo|sentry guard]].<ref name="On Program">{{InsiderCite|220|On Program}}</ref> In [[5 BBY]], he and his partner [[Kravas Drezzer]] were drinking at a [[Leisure Zone brothel|brothel]] in Morlana One's [[Leisure Zone]] when they spotted [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]], who was at the brothel in [[Search for Kerri|search]] of [[Kerri|his sister]].<ref name="Episode 1" /> The drunken pair<ref name="On Program" /> tailed Andor and attempted to rob him. However, Andor fought back, headbutting and accidentally [[Death|killing]] Skiff before executing Drezzer despite the man begging for his life.<ref name="Episode 1" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
Verlo Skiff first appeared in the [[Kassa (episode)|first episode]] of the [[Tony Gilroy]]'s live-action [[Disney+]] series ''[[Star Wars: Andor]]'', directed by [[Toby Haynes]]<ref name="Episode 1" /> and released on [[September 21]], [[2022]].<ref name="Trailer">{{SWYouTube|cKOegEuCcfw|Andor &#124; Official Trailer &#124; Disney+ (2:25)|sw_url=video/andor-official-trailer}}</ref> The character was portrayed by [[Stephen Wight]], with [[Mark Stanton-Kelly]] as his stunt double. His last name is not stated in the episode, but is mentioned in [[Aurebesh]] in [[Syril Karn]]'s report, which [[Chief Inspector]] [[Hyne]] reads on a [[datapad]].<ref name="Episode 1" />

